<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_SMyuJZhoYUivrtK-a57D_A_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_Tub6MaAr00WPMJVUR-obQA_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_7AY9sKkIU0iOTeU0r9gowA_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_I39tnRhEaUuTsv1TX4EfAw_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_idbHVsdIVUOvsD4EIe694g_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_0BoeJsYAEEm11nG88Ez-Zw_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_jVmZ5i8MWkGWmsAZh5g3lA_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_U70aKKz8OU6DDu0jXpkMxA_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_Vu-yokCnskCEpQai7kb6Jw_5_2"></a><a id="Tc_oMBUp8TRFEGXXECqffDD2g_5_5"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_TEMTy2iaF0Goi-x6b_nQzg_cont3"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Equity Award Modification</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On December 11, 2025, Arnout Ploos van Amstel notified the Company of his decision to resign from the Board of Directors and as a member of the Nominating and Governance Committee of the Board of Directors. The Board of Directors approved accelerated vesting of the unvested portion of two outstanding options, previously granted to Mr. Ploos van Amstel, relating to an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_12_11_2025_To_12_11_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_30D6AYwYwEKh7StfFeonVg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr_iZBOskGzn0ivZWVOGSxJZQ">41,549</ix:nonFraction> Class A Ordinary Shares, which became fully vested and exercisable on December 11, 2025. The Board of Directors also approved an extension of the post-termination exercise period of all of Mr. Ploos van Amstel&#8217;s vested share options to be <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_12_11_2025_To_12_11_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_30D6AYwYwEKh7StfFeonVg" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="zura:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsPostTerminationExercisePeriod" id="Narr_HKPnjjzNn0u4-iOMJR0_iQ">eighteen months</ix:nonNumeric> from the resignation date. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company recognized $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_hmVq-xIUzkukZgmYhfuChw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_MY4gjxGb60aceJ0sF5damg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" scale="6" id="Narr_InpOLwqrkU-MqOiVh-pWgA">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million of share-based compensation expense related to this modification within general and administrative expense in the consolidated statement of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On June 27, 2025, the Company and Verender Badial, the Company&#8217;s former Chief Financial Officer, entered into an agreement in connection with Mr. Badial&#8217;s resignation from the Company (the &#8220;Badial Settlement Agreement&#8221;). The Badial Settlement Agreement provides for accelerated vesting of the unvested portion of two outstanding options, previously granted to Mr. Badial, relating to an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_6_27_2025_To_6_27_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefFinancialOfficerMember_yqxNmHWo40-wEaDKZMzbMQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr_IZozkWe-xUi3VlhujUfPnw">198,540</ix:nonFraction> Class A Ordinary Shares, which became fully vested and exercisable on July 31, 2025. The Badial Settlement Agreement also provides for an extension of the post-termination exercise period of all of Mr. Badial&#8217;s vested share options to the applicable expiration date of the applicable share option, as of July 31, 2025, subject to certain conditions therein. All other remaining unvested options to purchase Class A Ordinary Shares were forfeited and cancelled on July 31, 2025. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company recognized $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_hmVq-xIUzkukZgmYhfuChw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefFinancialOfficerMember_XocdNSMu1EWT-QEKe8VRvg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" scale="6" id="Narr_og4VH0-Uy0Oxe2-MKmyF0w">0.2</ix:nonFraction> million of share-based compensation expense related to this modification within general and administrative expense in the consolidated statement of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On April 24, 2025, the Company amended a member of the Board of Director&#8217;s option agreements, causing his unvested options to purchase <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_4_24_2025_To_4_24_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_zura_AmendmentOfOptionAgreementsMember_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_us-gaap_AwardTypeAxis_us-gaap_EmployeeStockOptionMember_wGOB5LVHck6nTS_b7gInUA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr__4uvAAxHW0WxxkpQIDrnIA">32,099</ix:nonFraction> Class A Ordinary Shares to become fully vested and exercisable as of the AGM Date. Additionally, the Board of Directors extended the post-termination exercise period of his vested options to purchase an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_4_24_2025_To_4_24_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_zura_ExtensionOfPostTerminationExercisePeriodMember_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_UGCuhExfQUWdyP_thA4nyQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr__4XbiL6tv0aawCKZ1j6xyw">165,149</ix:nonFraction> Class A Ordinary Shares to the applicable expiration date of each of the respective option awards, upon completion of his service as a member of the Board of Directors. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company recognized $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_hmVq-xIUzkukZgmYhfuChw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_MY4gjxGb60aceJ0sF5damg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" scale="6" id="Narr_zCHrDlSG0kGfiGJfyJmXRw">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million of share-based compensation expense related to this modification within general and administrative expense in the consolidated statement of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On July 24, 2024, the Company entered into a settlement agreement with Someit Sidhu (&#8220;Sidhu Settlement Agreement&#8221;) in connection with the Chief Executive Officer (&#8220;CEO&#8221;) transition. Pursuant to the Sidhu Settlement Agreement, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_7_24_2024_To_7_24_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_tjZpD_scz0q0MYejILAPlQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr_fH1Wpme9IUyyhq7JfzKwTA">1,700,000</ix:nonFraction> share options became fully vested and immediately exercisable and the remaining <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="As_Of_7_24_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_KpqcbxdPdEyIsqAtdk7Fkw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedAndExpectedToVestOutstandingNumber" scale="0" id="Narr_3gllnd13zUKK3rwFzUOK9Q">250,000</ix:nonFraction> share options will vest annually over <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_24_2024_To_7_24_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_tjZpD_scz0q0MYejILAPlQ" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardAwardVestingPeriod1" id="Narr_hbn_COu1rk2O0wLVhGEq2g">three years</ix:nonNumeric> on the anniversary of the Sidhu Settlement Agreement. Accordingly, for the year ended December 31, 2024, the Company recorded $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_hmVq-xIUzkukZgmYhfuChw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_eMhST2nzVUa5JDMxYeHY8A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" scale="6" id="Narr_KC7zhSjhlEuLZ4O5vmNvKQ">5.9</ix:nonFraction> million of share-based compensation expense, in general and administrative expense in the consolidated statement of operations, for the remaining grant date fair value of the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_eMhST2nzVUa5JDMxYeHY8A" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr_RPJ0JFi4fUqKFqE2atCgyQ">1,700,000</ix:nonFraction> share options and the grant date fair value of the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_JK9NeBrBu0iOurVNx5GkXw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedAndExpectedToVestOutstandingNumber" scale="0" id="Narr_DjDRhZhCI0WSHELEaPxYng">250,000</ix:nonFraction> share options is being recorded to compensation expense over the revised vesting period. The Company determined that the Sidhu Settlement Agreement did not result in any incremental expense.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On January 10, 2024, the Company and its Chief Medical Officer (the &#8220;CMO&#8221;) entered into an agreement regarding the CMO&#8217;s departure from the Company (the &#8220;Severance Agreement&#8221;). In connection with the Severance Agreement, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_1_10_2024_To_1_10_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_zura_ChiefMedicalOfficerMember_qWTD_gH7bkOU1_YvD-Xyrg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardOptionsVestedNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="Narr_ApYtkxUcwUWCM0kTV7C_Wg">67,525</ix:nonFraction> of the share options previously granted to the CMO became fully vested and exercisable and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_B9wkd1v_sUeSSpxVjB0d7A" contextRef="Duration_1_10_2024_To_1_10_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_zura_ChiefMedicalOfficerMember_qWTD_gH7bkOU1_YvD-Xyrg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsVestedInPeriod" scale="0" id="Narr_yM0oEU3RTEmURKERWFtDNA">40,515</ix:nonFraction> of the RSUs previously granted to the CMO became fully vested. All remaining share options and RSUs not vested were forfeited and cancelled. During the year ended December 31, 2024, the Company recognized a reversal of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_hmVq-xIUzkukZgmYhfuChw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_zura_ChiefMedicalOfficerMember_w7D0qZEcG0ivc8aXQ5VdYg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zura:ShareBasedPaymentArrangementExpenseReversal" scale="6" id="Narr_lJHjTk0dRkKOzsImaYWwsQ">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million of share-based compensation expense related to this modification in research and development expense in the consolidated statement of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Share-based Compensation Expense</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Share-based compensation expense for all equity arrangements for the year ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 was as follows:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_ogZY1JNEk0KZygUCAut_Vg" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfCompensationCostForShareBasedPaymentArrangementsAllocationOfShareBasedCompensationCostsByPlanTableTextBlock" id="Tb_ZOV0RBqiCUCH0jrSTY-9AQ" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:71.44%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div st